--- BUF-01, BUF-05: declaration forms and exact capacity ---
a buffer called notebook.
If notebook's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-01: expected 0 got {notebook's size}", Exit 95. Print notebook's size.
a buffer called 'toolbox' is 80526 bytes in size.
If 'toolbox's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-01: expected 0 got {'toolbox's size}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox's size.
Print 0 minus 0.
If 'toolbox's capacity is not 80526 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-05: expected 80526 got {'toolbox's capacity}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox's capacity.
Print 'toolbox's size.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a buffer called notebook,
  If notebook's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-01: expected 0 got {notebook's size}", Exit 95. Print notebook's size,
  a buffer called 'toolbox' is 80526 bytes in size,
  If 'toolbox's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-01: expected 0 got {'toolbox's size}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox's size,
  Print 0 minus 0,
  If 'toolbox's capacity is not 80526 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-05: expected 80526 got {'toolbox's capacity}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox's capacity,
  Print 'toolbox's size.

--- BUF-10, BUF-11, BUF-12: size, length, capacity, empty ---
a buffer called 'the message slip' is 4097 bytes.
If 'the message slip's empty is false then, Print "ASSERT BUF-12: expected 1 got {'the message slip's empty}", Exit 95. Print 'the message slip's empty.
Print 0 add 0.
append "gldy87pskwgxv9f36zwhfu5no92s0" to 'the message slip'.
If 'the message slip's size is not 29 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-10: expected 29 got {'the message slip's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the message slip's size.
If 'the message slip's capacity is not 4097 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-10: expected 4097 got {'the message slip's capacity}", Exit 95. Print 'the message slip's capacity.
If 'the message slip's length is not 29 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-11: expected 29 got {'the message slip's length}", Exit 95. Print 'the message slip's length.
If 'the message slip's length is not 'the message slip's size then, Print "ASSERT BUF-11: expected {'the message slip's size} got {'the message slip's length}", Exit 95. Print 'the message slip's length.
If 'the message slip's empty then, Print "ASSERT BUF-12: expected 0 got {'the message slip's empty}", Exit 95. Print 'the message slip's empty.
Print 'the message slip's length.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a buffer called 'the message slip' is 4097 bytes,
  If 'the message slip's empty is false then, Print "ASSERT BUF-12: expected 1 got {'the message slip's empty}", Exit 95. Print 'the message slip's empty,
  Print 0 add 0,
  append "gldy87pskwgxv9f36zwhfu5no92s0" to 'the message slip',
  If 'the message slip's size is not 29 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-10: expected 29 got {'the message slip's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the message slip's size,
  If 'the message slip's capacity is not 4097 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-10: expected 4097 got {'the message slip's capacity}", Exit 95. Print 'the message slip's capacity,
  If 'the message slip's length is not 29 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-11: expected 29 got {'the message slip's length}", Exit 95. Print 'the message slip's length,
  If 'the message slip's length is not 'the message slip's size then, Print "ASSERT BUF-11: expected {'the message slip's size} got {'the message slip's length}", Exit 95. Print 'the message slip's length,
  If 'the message slip's empty then, Print "ASSERT BUF-12: expected 0 got {'the message slip's empty}", Exit 95. Print 'the message slip's empty,
  Print 'the message slip's length.

--- BUF-13: full, filled to capacity exactly ---
Create a buffer called 'the register' with size 32.
If 'the register's full then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 0 got {'the register's full}", Exit 95. Print 'the register's full.
append "sjqzlxnpnciv1zqmrbpt9t628l76ztov" to 'the register'.
If 'the register's full is false then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 1 got {'the register's full}", Exit 95. Print 'the register's full.
If 'the register's size is not 32 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 32 got {'the register's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the register's size.
a buffer called 'the mailbag'.
append "0aiz" to 'the mailbag'.
Print 'the mailbag's full.
Print 'the register's size.

--- BUF-13 again, a different split and a dynamic buffer ---
Create a buffer called 'the waybill' with size 63.
If 'the waybill's full then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 0 got {'the waybill's full}", Exit 95. Print 'the waybill's full.
append "tdq8y5ook" to 'the waybill'.
If 'the waybill's full then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 0 got {'the waybill's full}", Exit 95. Print 'the waybill's full.
append "nrr0hlbk6eu7qmxcq5mwv1ls4cqoe8stikzpu37nw3kqwvrc3zi4oe" to 'the waybill'.
If 'the waybill's full is false then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 1 got {'the waybill's full}", Exit 95. Print 'the waybill's full.
If 'the waybill's size is not 63 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 63 got {'the waybill's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the waybill's size.
Create a buffer called 'the shipping label'.
append "ninhe4ywd1mu14iu1rthrs1rqsq6" to 'the shipping label'.
Print 'the shipping label's full.
Print 'the waybill's size.

--- BUF-03: dynamic growth past the reserve ---
Create a buffer called 'the dispatch note'.
a number called 'the dispatch note appends made' is 0.
a boolean called 'the dispatch note overflowed' is false.
a boolean called 'the dispatch note found an error already pending' is false.
On error Set 'the dispatch note found an error already pending' to true.
While 'the dispatch note appends made' is less than 254, append "9mh4hquiihin0bcd97ygi23osc0r1it" to 'the dispatch note', On error Set 'the dispatch note overflowed' to true. Set 'the dispatch note appends made' to 'the dispatch note appends made' add 1.
If 'the dispatch note's size is not 7874 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-03: expected 7874 got {'the dispatch note's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note's size.
If 'the dispatch note overflowed' then, Print "ASSERT BUF-03: expected 0 got {'the dispatch note overflowed'}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note overflowed'.
Print 'the dispatch note's size.

--- BUF-07: a read that truncates, detected by size ---
a text called 'outgoing post path' is "{'the workspace'}/buffer1".
open a file for writing called 'outgoing post being written' at 'outgoing post path'.
Write "mbhx81qc3lmujkpvwn0u8zx9hy2vt7crlf05lrbj1mv9efd2" to 'outgoing post being written'.
Close 'outgoing post being written'.
open a file for reading called 'outgoing post being read' at 'outgoing post path'.
Create a buffer called 'outgoing post' with size 33.
a boolean called 'outgoing post was truncated' is false.
Read from 'outgoing post being read' into 'outgoing post'.
On error Set 'outgoing post was truncated' to true.
Close 'outgoing post being read'.
If 'outgoing post's size is not 33 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-07: expected 33 got {'outgoing post's size}", Exit 95. Print 'outgoing post's size.
If 'outgoing post's size is not 'outgoing post's capacity then, Print "ASSERT BUF-07: expected {'outgoing post's capacity} got {'outgoing post's size}", Exit 95. Print 'outgoing post's size.
Print 'outgoing post's size.

